1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:04,260
-爸爸 -你怎么起来了
- Daddy. - What are you doing up?

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:05,700
我睡不着
I can't sleep.

3
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,400
等等 你在我睡觉时吃东西吗
Wait. You eat while I'm in bed?

4
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:10,480
你们都背着我加餐吗
Is there a meal I don't know about?

5
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:11,120
加一两餐吧
A couple.

6
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:12,899
但你该就寝了 小家伙
But you need to hit the hay, buddy.

7
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:16,713
我要你鼾声如雷到辰时
I need you sawin' logs until 0700.

8
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:19,820
整段话我都不知道是什么意思
I don't know what any of that means.

9
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:23,020
最近 我和歌洛莉亚之间的"热情"有点冷却
Gloria and I are going through a romantic dry spell.

10
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,460
幸好 她今晚跟她朋友丽贝卡出去
Luckily, she's out tonight with her friend, Rebecca,

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,100
那女的嫁了个渣男
who is married to a jackass.

12
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:30,480
歌洛莉亚每次跟她见完面 都看我很顺眼
Gloria always comes home ready to show her appreciation.

13
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,720
忽然之间 我穿着袜子上床睡觉
Suddenly, me going to bed with socks on

14
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:34,573
也没那么十恶不赦了
is not such a deal-breaker.

15
00:00:36,968 --> 00:00:37,500
我靠
Aw, geez.

16
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,900
我回来了 杰
I'm home! Hey, Jay.

17
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,120
丽贝卡怎么样了
How's Rebecca?

18
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,959
她现在登上人生巅峰
She's never been better.

19
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:45,200
她一个月前离开了她老公
So, she left her husband like a month ago,

20
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,920
简直就像从肩膀上卸下了一个重担
and it's like a weight has been lifted off her shoulders.

21
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:49,900
说到肩膀
Speaking of shoulders,

22
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,700
你准备好享受我拿手的"按摩"了吗
are you ready for one of my famous massages?

23
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:52,720
不用了
No, I'm good.

24
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:55,280
是她打来
It's her.

25
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:55,760
喂
Hello?

26
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:58,240
那个服务生吗
The waiter?

27
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:02,057
我就知道他是在撩你
I knew he was flirting with you!

28
00:01:02,057 --> 00:01:04,840
别忘了她嫁的那个草包
Don't forget about that clod she married!

29
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:06,220
你算是觅得良缘了
You got one of the good guys!

30
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,800
而且他不用写下来都能记住我们点的菜
And he didn't have to write down our order,

31
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,900
他以后肯定也不会忘了你的生日
so you know that he won't forget your birthday.

32
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:19,500
乔把所有玩具都丢在地上了
Joe leaves all his toys on the floor.

33
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,780
我叫他捡起来 但他都不听话
I tell him to pick them up, but he doesn't listen.

34
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:26,060
我跟你说 卧室里就是一场灾难
I'm telling you, it's a disaster in the bedroom.

35
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,940
我不知道如何是好
I don't know what to do.

36
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:31,280
就像是他不记得"东西"该往哪儿塞
It's like he can't remember where things go.

37
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,760
最终 我沮丧失望
Eventually, I get so frustrated

38
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,000
只好自己"搞定"了
that I take care of it myself.

39
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:37,800
打屁股
Spanking?

40
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,980
行吧 或许可以试试这招
Well, yeah, I guess we could try that.

41
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,140
其实你说起这事
Actually, now that you mention it,

42
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:45,749
哈维尔和我很久以前也试过
Javier and I tried it a long time ago.

43
00:01:45,749 --> 00:01:47,461
确实改变局面了
It was a game-changer.

44
00:01:48,869 --> 00:01:51,820
丽贝卡现在过得很好
Ay. Rebecca is doing so well.

45
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:52,820
听起来她在纵享人生
Sounds like she's having fun.

46
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:55,980
海军过去强迫我们看关于她那种女人的电影
Navy used to make us watch films about girls like that.

47
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:59,720
她老公从来都没真正满足过她的需求
Well, her husband never really gave her what she needed.

48
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:00,556
她有告诉他吗
Did she tell him?

49
00:02:00,556 --> 00:02:04,040
没有 但有时跟一个不用你说
No. But sometimes it's more exciting to be with someone

50
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:07,520
就知道你想要什么的人在一起 比较刺激
that already knows what you want without you telling them.

51
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:08,440
懂了
Got it.

52
00:02:09,246 --> 00:02:10,096
喂
Ay! Hey!

53
00:02:10,229 --> 00:02:12,040
搞什么啊
Wh-What the hell was that?!

54
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,000
没什么 你知道吗
Nothing! You know what?

55
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,460
我好像忘记锁大门了
I think I forgot to lock the front door.

56
00:02:28,972 --> 00:02:31,100
-他回来啦 -别生气
- There he is. - Oh, now, don't get mad.

57
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:33,120
我知道我之前说只会为派对买郁金香
I know I said I was only getting tulips for the party,

58
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,845
但我豪气了一把 买了兰花
but I splurged and I got orchids.

59
00:02:34,845 --> 00:02:36,640
-我也希望这个派对与众不同啊 -好吧
- I -- I wanted the party to be special, too. ?- Okay.

60
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:38,820
我解释一下 我之前不知道你会买兰花
And in my defense, I didn't know about the orchids.

61
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:40,500
我买了台钢琴
I got a piano.

62
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,000
真的吗 在哪里
Really, where?

63
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,559
我最近得到了一份很体面的工作
I recently got a pretty fancy job

64
00:02:44,559 --> 00:02:47,385
给亿万富翁迈克尔·奎因利打工
working for billionaire Michael Quinly.

65
00:02:47,385 --> 00:02:49,080
-有点厉害 -就是很厉害
- It's kind of a big deal. - It is a big deal.

66
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,780
我承认 举办派对
Now, admittedly, throwing a party

67
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:54,160
庆祝自己走好运了 可能有点炫耀的意味
to celebrate your own reversal of fortune could be seen as braggy.

68
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:56,240
有点算是灰姑娘卖瓜了
Sort of a rags-to-bitches story, if you will.

69
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,100
但话说回头 之前好一阵
Then again, for a while now,

70
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:00,060
每当我告诉朋友我为工作烦恼时
when I've been telling my friends that I was struggling,

71
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:01,940
他们都会露出"那个眼神"
they'd give me "That look" --

72
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:03,760
大部分是同情
the one that's mostly sympathetic

73
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,860
但又掺杂了一丝看好戏的感觉
with just a touch of enjoying my pain.

74
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:09,560
所以今天 我会得到另一种眼神
So, today, I get the other look --

75
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:12,140
大部分是"我真为你高兴"
the one that's mostly "I'm so happy for you"

76
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:14,660
但又掺杂了一丝"妒忌使我丑陋"的感觉
with just a hint of "I am wracked with jealousy."

77
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,400
见到以前那群朋友会很开心的
It'll be good to see the old gang again.

78
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,970
-是啊 没错 -嗯
- Yeah. Yeah, yeah. - Yeah.

79
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:23,580
你好呀
Hey, you.

80
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:26,620
你在干嘛 跟男生发短信吗
What's going on? You, uh -- you texting a boy?

81
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,040
只是在考虑我夏天的计划
Just figuring out my summer plans.

82
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:29,593
我还记得我大一那年的夏天
I remember the summer of my junior year.

83
00:03:29,593 --> 00:03:31,677
我跟着NWA乐队的巡演
I followed N.W.A. on tour --

84
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:32,960
NWA就是"弹手风琴的内村人"
Nebraskans With Accordions.

85
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:35,580
当然了 这是团员惨遭谋杀之前的事了
This was before Polka Pete was brutally murdered, of course.

86
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,080
我的有点不同
Yeah, this is a little different.

87
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,420
事实上我想去麻省理工实习
I'm actually up for an internship

88
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:41,654
研究最小超对称标准模型
researching the minimal supersymmetric standard model at M.I.T.

89
00:03:41,883 --> 00:03:44,520
酷哦 去波士顿
Cool. Beantown.

90
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,660
我不知道我为什么像小女生一样紧张期待
I don't know why I'm getting all girly and excited about it.

91
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:47,900
反正我也不可能得到这个机会
It's not like I'm gonna get it anyways.

92
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,540
怎么说丧气话呢 如果你想听我的建议...
What's with the quitter talk? If you want my advice --

93
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:51,620
并不想 不过谢了
No, I don't, but thanks.

94
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,520
怎么一堆垃圾食品
What is all this junk?

95
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,620
水果卷 薯片 巧克力牛奶
Fruit Roll-ups, chips, chocolate milk? Ugh.

96
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:57,409
冰箱里啥吃的都没有
Th-There's nothing in the fridge.

97
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,840
我给你准备一盒午餐带走
I'm packing you a lunch.

98
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:02,060
我总是听说人生到了某个阶段
I've always heard there comes a time in life

99
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:04,540
就会变成由孩子反过来照顾父母
when the kid starts parenting the parents.

100
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,680
我本来以为那是我40岁之后才会发生的事
I thought it would be when I was in my 40s.

101
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,500
但我有超越年龄的成熟
But I'm pretty mature for my age,

102
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:10,420
而我爸拿到薯格都会开心地拍手
and my dad claps when he gets waffle fries.

103
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,860
你为什么还在家里
What are you even still doing home?

104
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,900
平时这会儿你不是已经去魔术店了吗
Don't you usually open your magic shop by now?

105
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:15,720
对 我只是晚去一点
Yeah. I'm just going in a little late.

106
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,280
听起来对生意可不好
Doesn't sound good for business.

107
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:19,240
而且我看到你偷偷把胡萝卜从午餐里取出来了
And I saw you sneak those carrots out of your lunch.

108
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,620
我是想避开另一位店主
I'm trying to avoid one of the other shop owners.

109
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:23,840
那家伙有点吓人
Kind of an intimidating character.

110
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,780
一切始于一个停车位引发的争执
It started with a dispute over a parking space

111
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:26,877
之后矛盾就升级了
and escalated from there.

112
00:04:26,877 --> 00:04:30,340
我们家的人从来不躲避恶霸
Hey...we don't avoid bullies in this family.

113
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:32,040
我们勇敢面对他们
We stand up to them.

114
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:33,700
去吧
Off you go.

115
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:36,160
我想你没意识到我面对的是什么狠角色
I don't think you realize what kind of person I'm up against.

116
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:37,580
昨天 他把我全部恶作剧漏洞杯
Yesterday, all my dribble glasses

117
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:39,080
全换成了真杯子
were replaced with real ones.

118
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,380
丢死人了
It was humiliating.

119
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:43,720
朗吉 我们得好好聊聊最近的事
So, Long', we have a lot to catch up on.

120
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:45,040
-最近怎么样[什么升了] -我的体重没升
- What's up? - Not my weight.

121
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,999
汤姆·布拉迪节食法改变了我看待世界的方式
The Tom Brady diet changed the way I see the world.

122
00:04:47,999 --> 00:04:51,480
食物 非食物 超级食物 毒药
Food, not food, super-food, poison.

123
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,140
你的新鲜事就聊完了
Oh, well, okay, that covers you.

124
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,300
我想问你近况
I was going to ask about you,

125
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,940
但你知道 我总是为你的答案紧张
but, you know, I'm always nervous about the answer.

126
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,356
我们来碰碰运气吧
Well, you know what? Let's roll the dice.

127
00:04:58,356 --> 00:04:59,998
-原来我... -米奇
- So, it turns out that I -- - Hey, Mitch.

128
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:01,540
小卡在哪
Where's Cam?

129
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,380
克莱尔 真是惊喜
Claire, what a surprise.

130
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:05,340
你说什么呢
What are you talking about?

131
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,597
是你让我给你带钢琴曲的
You asked me to bring over the piano music.

132
00:05:06,597 --> 00:05:07,940
《派对时光最爱金曲》
"Party-time Favorites."

133
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:09,320
天啊 真是无巧不成书啊
Oh, my gosh, how apropos.

134
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,840
我去放在家里的新钢琴上
I'll just set these on our new piano... ?

135
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:13,740
这我刚好会的乐器上
...that I know how to play.

136
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:15,580
派对很棒 各位
Great party, boys.

137
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,080
这钢琴这么显眼不聊不行吧
We need to talk about the piano in the room.

138
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:20,280
好吧 是这样
Uh, well, yes, so, okay, okay.

139
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:21,800
小卡一直想要一台钢琴
So, Cam has always wanted one,

140
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:24,280
说实话 我们一直负担不起
and frankly, it has been out of our price range

141
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,820
直到这周
until this week.

142
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:28,340
有趣的故事 原来我...
Fun story. It turns out that I --

143
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:29,060
我真没礼貌
I'm being rude.

144
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,660
我是山姆·特恩布尔
Sam Turnbull.

145
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,380
我是克莱尔·邓菲
Oh! Claire Dunphy.

146
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:34,860
你是《洛杉矶女性》杂志的编辑 对吧
Hi. You are the editor of L.A. Woman magazine, right?

147
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:37,260
发音应该是"拉乌芒"[法语]
I believe it's pronounced "La Woman."

148
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:37,940
才不是
It isn't.

149
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:41,100
真有趣 因为你办公室上周给我公司打了电话
It's funny because your office called my business last week.

150
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:43,860
貌似我出现在《商业女性》特辑的
Apparently, I'm on some short list

151
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:45,380
最终候选人名单上
for the Women in Business issue.

152
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,300
-是橱柜业吧 -是的
- Closets, right? - Yeah.

153
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,759
我打破女人无法在高位的"玻璃天花板"
I shattered the glass ceiling --

154
00:05:48,759 --> 00:05:52,340
很讽刺的是 我们出了一款新的玻璃天花板橱柜
and ironically, we have a new glass-ceiling closet.

155
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:54,020
你穿衣服时能看外面是否下雨
You can see if it's raining when you're getting dressed.

156
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,320
会拯救许多小山羊皮
Gonna save a lot of suede.

157
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:58,240
今年竞争很激烈啊
Well, it's, um, pretty competitive this year.

158
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,840
我要去找钢琴另一边的人聊聊天
Anyway, I'm meeting someone on the other side of the piano.

159
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,260
我该走了
I should leave now.

160
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:07,999
我都对他的傻逼杂志没兴趣
I don't even care about his stupid magazine,

161
00:06:07,999 --> 00:06:09,520
但被他这么甩脸就走...
but to be dismissed like that?

162
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:12,738
各位 感谢你们光临寒舍
Hey, everyone, everyone. Thank you so much for coming.

163
00:06:12,738 --> 00:06:14,930
大家现在都好难有机会见面
We never get to see each other anymore,

164
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:16,740
大家的生活都很忙
what with our busy lives.

165
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:19,600
乔撒姆忙于环境音乐作曲
And Jotham's ambient music compositions,

166
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,980
迪帕克致力于游击园艺
and, uh, Deepak's guerrilla gardening,

167
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:26,303
还有我和我的新工作
and, well, me and my big new job

168
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:27,815
老板是迈克尔·奎恩利
working for Michael Quinly.

169
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:28,720
是啊
Yeah.

170
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:31,341
在各大博物馆都能看到他名字的有钱人吗
The rich guy whose name is on all those museums?

171
00:06:31,341 --> 00:06:34,121
还有医院 敬我们所有人
And hospitals, yeah. So, to all of us!

172
00:06:35,095 --> 00:06:36,770
恭喜啊
Ah, congratulations.

173
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,200
真棒 我们都
It's really great. We're all --

174
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,420
我们都为你高兴
We're all so happy for you.

175
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:41,540
谢谢 谢谢
Thank you. Thank you.

176
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,080
你看见了大家的表情 对吧
You saw the look, right?

177
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:48,040
完全是爱和支持 夹杂了一丝讨厌的嫉妒
Pure love and support with just a hint of rancid envy.

178
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:48,980
来聊聊
A word.

179
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,280
但我正在爽呢 小卡
But I'm basking. Um, Cam.

180
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:53,240
你说话时我上了网
So, while you were talking, I got online,

181
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:56,642
你的新老板被发现挪用公款了
and...your new boss was caught embezzling.

182
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:57,960
你的公司要倒闭了
Your company is crumbling.

183
00:06:58,100 --> 00:07:00,940
不不 这事不能又发生在我身上
No! No! This -- This can't be happening to me again.

184
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:03,242
相信我 你会找到别的工作
You know what? You'll find something else.

185
00:07:03,242 --> 00:07:04,280
天啊 小卡 我十秒前
Oh, my -- Cam, I literally

186
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,340
刚吹嘘了一份并不存在的工作
just bragged about a job that doesn't exist.

187
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:08,240
好吧 他们不能发现这事
Okay, okay. They cannot know,

188
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,221
否则这会变成同情派对
or else this will turn into an actual pity party.

189
00:07:10,221 --> 00:07:12,000
好 交给我吧
Okay. Yeah. Yeah, yeah. I-I got this.

190
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:12,880
各位
Hi, everyone.

191
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:16,080
我们要更深层 更私密地
So, we are about to get to know one another on a deeper,

192
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,980
了解彼此
more personal level.

193
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:20,140
我想你们都知道这个碗是装什么的
I think you all know what the bowl is for.

194
00:07:20,869 --> 00:07:24,040
不 不是钥匙 乔撒姆
Hey, no. Not your keys, Jotham.

195
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:24,880
是手机
Your phones!

196
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:28,000
我们要重拾失落已久的谈话艺术
We are about to rediscover the long-lost art of conversation.

197
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,380
如果保姆打来电话呢
What if the sitter calls?

198
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:32,000
你的狗狗会没事的 先生们 请交出手机
Your dog will be fine. Phones, gentlemen, phones.

199
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,100
你周六都上班吗
You're working on a Saturday?

200
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,920
我在面对一点小问题
I've been dealing with a little problem.

201
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:41,421
这种时候 我只会去一个地方寻求帮助
In moments like this, there's only one place I turn.

202
00:07:41,421 --> 00:07:43,434
我受宠若惊 爸爸
Well, I am flattered, Dad.

203
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:44,700
好吧
Right.

204
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:47,960
既然你在这里
Hey, but, you know, since you're here...

205
00:07:49,202 --> 00:07:50,502
这话题很难开口
Uh, it's a difficult subject.

206
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,420
歌洛莉亚和我的
Gloria and I...

207
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:55,360
床事有点问题
...having an issue in the bedroom.

208
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:56,658
好吧
Okay.

209
00:07:56,658 --> 00:07:59,874
速度和强度都不如从前
There's been a drop-off of pace and intensity.

210
00:07:59,874 --> 00:08:01,280
我了解到她想要
I get the impression she's looking for,

211
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,438
换换口味
maybe, a little more variety.

212
00:08:02,438 --> 00:08:03,615
但也不能怪她
But you can't blame her.

213
00:08:03,615 --> 00:08:05,820
我的那几招从70年代开始就一直在用
I've been using the same moves since the '70s.

214
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:07,357
我干脆加点70年代舞步进去得了
I may as well be doing "The Hustle" in there.

215
00:08:07,357 --> 00:08:09,580
我要润润嗓子
I'm just gonna wet my whistle.

216
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:11,220
我听见她昨晚跟她的朋友说
I heard her tell her friend last night

217
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:12,380
想被打屁股
about wanting to be spanked.

218
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:17,120
不久后 机会出现在眼前
And later, the opportunity presented itself, and...

219
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,238
不 你没有 你没有
No, you didn't. You didn't.

220
00:08:18,238 --> 00:08:20,136
-三次 -天啊 为什么是三次 爸爸
- Three times. - Oh, God. Why three times, Dad?

221
00:08:20,136 --> 00:08:22,200
我不知道 也许因为多年来
I don't know. Maybe all those years of ping-pong

222
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,640
我在仓库打了不少乒乓球 手腕很灵活
in the warehouse. I've got very agile wrists.

223
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:26,860
但我不知道该怎么挽回这场面了
But I don't know how I come back from this one.

224
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:29,060
爸爸
Well, uh, Dad, when you, um --

225
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,660
当你对歌洛莉亚做那件事时
When you did what you did to Gloria,

226
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:34,300
你让性爱的重点全聚焦在她身体上了
you made the sex all about her body,

227
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:36,400
而女人希望能照顾到她们心灵
and a woman wants it to be about the mind.

228
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,595
糟糕 我就害怕是这种狗屁
Oh, crap. I was afraid it would be about that sort of thing.

229
00:08:39,595 --> 00:08:42,880
听着 她是个聪明有趣的女人
Look, she is an intelligent, interesting woman.

230
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:45,221
你得提醒她你注意到了这些
And you just need to remind her that you notice that --

231
00:08:45,221 --> 00:08:47,520
不像是《洛杉矶女性》杂志
unlike, say, I don't know, L.A. Woman magazine,

232
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,860
只关注女人的外表
that only cares about how a woman looks.

233
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,940
所以不聊我的事了
So, we're off my thing, huh?

234
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,160
没错 希望永远别再提
Hopefully forever, yes.

235
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:53,960
我今天在小卡和米奇那
I ran into the editor of that magazine

236
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:56,140
碰到了那个杂志的编辑 你知道吗
over at Cam and Mitch's today, and you know what?

237
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,320
他上下打量我
He looks me up and down.

238
00:08:57,320 --> 00:09:00,050
突然我就不在他们的商界女士名单上了
Suddenly, I am off their women-in-business list.

239
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:02,240
现在《洛杉矶女性》有自己的杂志啦
So, L.A. Woman is its own magazine now?

240
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:04,860
我记得它以前是在《洛杉矶男性》的末尾
I remember when it was the back page of L.A. Man.

241
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:08,160
我想我是没琳达·沃恩那么美
Well, I suppose I'm just not as glamorous as Linda Vaughn,

242
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:10,120
矫正鞋女王
the queen of corrective shoes.

243
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:12,580
这和你穿的
And this has nothing to do with the fact that you showed up

244
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,560
像刚给马喂过水一样有关吧
looking like someone who just watered some horses?

245
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,179
那又怎样 实力呢
Who cares? What about merit?

246
00:09:16,179 --> 00:09:18,260
我知道 但你得遵守游戏规则
I hear you. But you got to play the game.

247
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:19,438
我上《橱柜日报》
I didn't get on the cover

248
00:09:19,438 --> 00:09:22,278
78年9月的封面
of Closet Time's September '78 issue

249
00:09:22,278 --> 00:09:25,540
可不是因为穿了不合身的牛仔裤
by wearing Jordache jeans one size too big.

250
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,840
我才不这样
I'm not doing it.

251
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,300
他们搞他们的选美比赛吧
They can keep their beauty contest.

252
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:28,920
我不在乎
I don't care.

253
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,380
在你说不之前 先看看这个
Before you say "No", take a look at this.

254
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:35,060
这不能证明你要证明的 爸
It's not making the case you think it's making, Dad.

255
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:37,120
天啊
Oh, God.

256
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:41,660
所有的手机都在这了
Okay, that's all the phones.

257
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,840
在聚会结束前
Look, nobody's gonna find out about you losing your job

258
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:44,780
不会有人发现你失业了
until after the party.

259
00:09:45,377 --> 00:09:47,160
好 我去开门
Okay, I'm -- I'm gonna get that.

260
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:49,000
你打电话退了
You call someone about returning the piano

261
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:50,080
我们承担不起的钢琴
we can no longer afford.

262
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:53,260
其实你的新工作也养不起它
Well, we couldn't really afford it with your new job, either.

263
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:57,340
你怎么不回我短信
Why haven't you been texting me back?

264
00:09:58,795 --> 00:10:00,920
-你心里鄙视我们呢吧 -没
- You're judging us, aren't you? ?- No.

265
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:03,499
这和我听说的你俩做的
This is nothing compared to the things that I have heard

266
00:10:03,499 --> 00:10:05,185
-根本没法比 -好吧 等下
- that you two do - Okay, whoa, whoa, whoa.

267
00:10:05,185 --> 00:10:06,480
我没看到你的短信
I-I never saw your text, okay?

268
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,580
我们电话都放在大碗里
All of our phones are in a bowl.

269
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:09,760
是"那种"聚会啊
Oh, it's that kind of party.

270
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:11,500
你觉得我们在干啥啊
What do you think that we do?

271
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:12,598
我遇到问题了
I have a problem.

272
00:10:12,598 --> 00:10:14,134
等会吧 我有客人呢
Well, can it wait? I have guests.

273
00:10:14,134 --> 00:10:16,256
你爸打我屁屁
Your father spanked me.

274
00:10:16,256 --> 00:10:17,844
自助餐 他们可以自助啦
Eh, it's a buffet. They'll be fine.

275
00:10:17,844 --> 00:10:20,060
我和钢琴公司说了
Okay, I talked to the piano company --

276
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:21,820
嗯 我爸打她屁屁了 我们就说到这
Okay, okay, my dad spanked her. You're all caught up.

277
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:23,660
-什么 -你做什么了
- What? - What did you do?

278
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,860
我大叫 然后他跑了
I screamed, he ran away.

279
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:27,700
现在我觉得他有点窘迫
And now I think he's embarrassed.

280
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:28,840
好吧 好吧
Okay, okay.

281
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:31,840
不晓得真假 但有时人们这么对别人
For what it's worth, sometimes people do things to other people

282
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,720
可能是希望别人这么对自己
that they want done to themselves.

283
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,080
有时 连续好多年
Sometimes, for years on end.

284
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:37,160
真的吗
Really?

285
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:41,460
你觉得杰想让我打他屁屁
So, you think that Jay wants me to spank him?

286
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,580
如果他像我交往过的
Well, if he's like some of the successful,

287
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:45,660
那些成功男士 那就是的
powerful men I've been with, yes.

288
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,940
-那些男士是谁 -我不做的事是哪些
- Who are those men? - What are these things I don't do?

289
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:51,020
我想我可以问问那是不是他想要的
Well, I guess I could ask him if that's what he wants.

290
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:52,554
不不不 别那么做
No, no, no, no, no. Don't do that.

291
00:10:52,554 --> 00:10:54,880
他可能已经觉得难为情了
He's probably already feeling self-conscious.

292
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:57,020
自然点 就好像没发生过一样
Act casual, like it never happened.

293
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,320
我做得到
I can do that.

294
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:01,220
你们这个超级大的钢琴
I haven't even said anything

295
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:03,280
我就什么都没说
about this gigantic piano you have here.

296
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:06,380
如果今天退不了 它就真属于咱们了
Okay. Well, if it doesn't go back today, we own it,

297
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:07,740
搬家公司马上就到
so the moving company is on the way.

298
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,920
我觉得我们的客人会看到的
Okay, well, I think our guests are gonna notice that,

299
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,580
可能会好奇为什么
maybe ask a question or two.

300
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:12,440
我来处理
I've got this.

301
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:14,480
各位 各位
Hey, guys. Hi, guys.

302
00:11:14,660 --> 00:11:15,779
米奇尔和我
Mitchell and I...

303
00:11:15,779 --> 00:11:17,300
可能就只有小卡 还不确定
Or maybe just Cam. Not sure yet.

304
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:20,060
要重新装修我们的浴室 我们想问
...are about to remodel our bathroom, and we were wondering,

305
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:24,572
有哪位对于室内装修有强烈看法
does anyone here have strong opinions about interior design?

306
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,402
好的 请各位跟我来
Okay. Can you guys, uh, follow me right this way?

307
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,509
都请进 空间很大的
All right, everybody in. Yep, there's plenty of room.

308
00:11:30,509 --> 00:11:32,220
我关上门
And I'll -- I'll just close the door,

309
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:34,940
给你们点空间 这样就能畅所欲言
give you guys some privacy so you can speak freely.

310
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:36,020
好啦
There you go.

311
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,460
好啦 看啊
All right. And, oh, look at that.

312
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,833
门把手掉了
The...doorknob came off.

313
00:11:40,833 --> 00:11:42,685
你们等下 我去修一下
Sit tight. I got to fix this.

314
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:43,900
爸
Hey, Dad.

315
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:46,040
宝贝 你在这干嘛
Hey, sweetie. What are you doing here?

316
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,480
你真觉得我不会发现这些胡萝卜吗
Did you really think I wouldn't notice these?

317
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,920
还有 我拿到了那个实习机会
Also, I got that internship.

318
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,900
需要你在保险单上签个字
I just need your signature on my insurance form.

319
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:54,160
我和你说了要保持乐观
I told you to stay positive.

320
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:55,800
这会多么有趣呀
How much fun is this gonna be?

321
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,820
这跟有趣完全无关
It's really not about fun.

322
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,298
会有很多辛苦的工作
It's gonna be a lot of hard work.

323
00:11:59,298 --> 00:12:00,799
压力爆表
The pressure's off the charts.

324
00:12:00,799 --> 00:12:03,100
难怪有心理健康免责同意书
Well, that would explain the mental-health waiver.

325
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:05,340
上一个他们录取的大学生完全崩溃了
The last undergrad they let into the program completely snapped.

326
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:06,900
他们发现她在自由之路[观光行程]上
They found her wandering the Freedom Trail

327
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:08,660
啥也没穿就戴个护眼镜瞎逛
wearing nothing but her safety goggles.

328
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:12,860
邓菲 你又占了我的位置
Dunphy, you're in my spot again.

329
00:12:13,060 --> 00:12:14,920
-就是她 -她就是欺负你的家伙吗
- That's her. - She's your bully?

330
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,841
你知道她根本就没多壮吧
You realize she's not even that big, right?

331
00:12:16,841 --> 00:12:18,076
只是头发蓬
It's mostly just hair.

332
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:19,900
这矮冬瓜是谁
Who's the jock?

333
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:22,620
斯蒂芬妮 这是我女儿艾丽克斯
Oh, Stephanie, this is my daughter Alex.

334
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:24,159
艾丽克斯 这是斯蒂芬妮
Uh, Alex, this is Stephanie.

335
00:12:24,159 --> 00:12:26,260
她是隔壁棋盘游戏店的老板
She owns the board-game shop next door.

336
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:28,360
对 我卖卡牌游戏《魔法风云会》[魔术集合]
Yeah. I sell "Magic: The Gathering",

337
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,840
他卖魔术 但没人来集合
and he sells magic, and no one is gathering.

338
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:31,700
要不要这样
Come on.

339
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:33,900
爸 记得我们聊过的吗
Dad, remember what we talked about.

340
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:37,340
记得 严格来说
Oh, yeah. Technically...

341
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,938
9号位是个共享的停车位
...spot nine is a shared parking space.

342
00:12:40,938 --> 00:12:44,820
看谁消失的球[胆子]回来了
Ooh, look whose disappearing balls came back.

343
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:47,020
我们通过新出的珍藏版
What do you say we settle this once and for all

344
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:48,900
《巫师和术士》来永久解决这个问题吧
with the newly released collector's edition

345
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:50,060
你觉得怎么样
of "Wizards and Warlocks"?

346
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:50,960
来吧
Set her up.

347
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:53,300
我受够你的欺负了
I'm done being pushed around by you.

348
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,258
谁赢了车位就归谁
Winner gets the spot.

349
00:12:54,258 --> 00:12:55,686
这是个角色扮演游戏
It's a role-playing game.

350
00:12:55,686 --> 00:12:57,360
我是佐艾尔 十九级巫师
I'm Zorel, a 19th-level wizard

351
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,738
有三十个金元宝和一头曾是我儿子的牛
with 30 gold ingots and a cow who used to be my son.

352
00:12:59,738 --> 00:13:02,020
这游戏我熟 我可是加州理工的学生
I'm familiar with the game. I go to Cal-Tech.

353
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:04,020
发明这游戏的人去年给我们做了毕业演讲
The guy who invented it gave our commencement speech last year.

354
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:04,889
来吧 邓菲
Okay, Dunphy.

355
00:13:04,889 --> 00:13:07,601
接着上次玩 你卖了你的长剑
When we left off, you had just sold your long sword

356
00:13:07,601 --> 00:13:09,440
-买了些豆子 -本可能是魔豆的
- for some beans. - Which could've been magic.

357
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:10,900
从没有迹象表明那是魔豆
There was no indication of that.

358
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,280
爸 你的金子都哪去了
Dad, where's all your gold?

359
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:14,140
我发现佐艾尔不喜欢被太多身外之物
I found that Zorel doesn't like to be weighed down

360
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:15,500
拖慢脚步
by too many worldly possessions.

361
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:18,480
但胜负的关键是尽快掠夺并用金子换武器
But the key is to pillage early and trade your gold for weapons

362
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:20,700
赶在范维寇大门打开放出食人魔之前换好
before the Van Wickle gates open and the ogres are released.

363
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:23,760
诅咒卡 你的双手变成蹄子了
Curse card. Your hands are now hooves.

364
00:13:24,045 --> 00:13:24,960
该你扔了
Your roll.

365
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,649
但先让我做个提议
Uh, but first, a proposal --

366
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,600
用我的盾换你的羽毛帽
my shield for your feathered cap.

367
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:31,640
我看不下去了 骰子给我 起来
I can't watch this. Give me those. Up.

368
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:39,220
我知道你的打算了
Ah, I see where you're going with this --

369
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:41,300
你要呼吁议会长老召开和平会议
calling for a peace conference with the council of elders.

370
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,420
不 我要把议会长老送到船上
No. I'm putting the council of elders on our ships

371
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,620
烧死他们 扔吧
and burning them. Go.

372
00:13:46,332 --> 00:13:50,020
我在这 随意读读杂志 杰
I'm here, casually reading a magazine, Jay.

373
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:51,260
不愧是我的天才
There's my brainiac.

374
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:52,700
你都不用回头看
You didn't even have to turn around.

375
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:53,440
就知道是我
You knew it was me.

376
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:55,261
曼尼在学校
Oh, well, Manny's at school,

377
00:13:55,261 --> 00:13:57,459
乔又没有钥匙
and Joe doesn't have a key, so...

378
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:58,700
你在研读什么
What are you tearing through?

379
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:01,220
没什么 不过是本时尚杂志
Nothing. Just, like, a fashion magazine.

380
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,340
英语的 你的第二语言
In English, your second language.

381
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,680
你脑袋里有那么多信息
With all that information in your head,

382
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,540
我们该叫你"百事通布朗"[棕色]
we should be calling you "Encyclopedia Brown" --

383
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:09,560
我这么说可与你的肤色无关
which sounds like a slur, but isn't.

384
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:10,820
你肯定能帮我解决
Hey, I'll bet you can help

385
00:14:10,820 --> 00:14:12,200
一个困扰了我很久的难题
me with something I've been struggling with.

386
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:13,060
我看不太可能
I doubt it.

387
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:15,280
让我惊喜一下 出手吧
Give me a thrill. Take a whack at it.

388
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,460
你到底想让我做什么
What exactly do you want me to do?

389
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,480
我相信你能解读这个线索
I'm sure you can figure out this clue.

390
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,580
来 就填一行[打一下] 帮我开个头
Come on, one across. Help me get started.

391
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,240
什么鬼
What the hell?!

392
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,780
什么鬼
What the hell?!

393
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,480
我会整理房间的 我保证
I'll clean my room, I promise!

394
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:36,660
可恶
Damn it.

395
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,880
你到达埃克斯莫尔峰会了
You made it to the Summit of Exmore.

396
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:40,060
真有那个峰会吗
It exists?

397
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:43,093
如果我想得到这个实习机会
I need to get these forms in by 5:00

398
00:14:43,093 --> 00:14:44,760
我得在五点前把表格送到
if I'm gonna take this internship,

399
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:45,980
我当然想得到
which I obviously am

400
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:47,720
因为我已经为这努力一辈子了
because I've been working for this my entire life.

401
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:50,520
爸 交给你了 你基本上稳赢不输了
Dad, take over. You're basically in an unlosable position.

402
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,380
你来到了一个十字路口
You appear to be at a crossroads --

403
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:56,960
在峰会大门与守卫决斗
battle the guards at the summit gate

404
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,400
还是进入未知领域的传送门
or take a portal to lands unknown.

405
